            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you own or operate a semi truck, you already know one thing for certain: maintenance is not optional.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "It's one of the largest and most predictable expenses in your operation, and it directly impacts uptime, safety, and profitability. Yet many owner-operators and fleet managers still underestimate the average maintenance cost for a semi truck, or struggle to understand where those dollars really go.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we work with Florida-based owner-operators and fleets every day. One of the most common conversations we have is about controlling semi truck maintenance costs without cutting corners that lead to bigger problems later. Let's break down what maintenance truly costs, what drives those numbers, and how the right parts and service strategy can protect your long-term ROI.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-average-cost",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Is the Average Maintenance Cost for a Semi Truck?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "average-cost"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-average-cost-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "On average, the cost to maintain a semi truck ranges from <strong>$15,000 to $25,000 per year per truck</strong>, depending on mileage, usage, truck age, and service habits. For high-mileage trucks, annual maintenance can climb even higher, especially when preventive care is delayed or parts quality is compromised.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "stats-average-cost-2",
                  "type": "statBand",
                  "props": {
                    "stats": [
                      {
                        "value": "$15,000–$25,000",
                        "label": "Typical annual maintenance cost per truck"
                      },
                      {
                        "value": "$15K vs $30K",
                        "label": "The gap between two similar trucks often comes down to service decisions, not luck"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-average-cost-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The key takeaway? Maintenance is unavoidable, but unplanned maintenance is what really hurts.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-cost-breakdown",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Breaking Down Semi Truck Maintenance Costs",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "cost-breakdown"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-breakdown-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding your truck repair cost breakdown helps you plan smarter and avoid surprises. While every operation is different, most maintenance expenses fall into these core categories.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-cost-breakdown-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive Maintenance and Inspections",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-breakdown-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Routine services like oil changes, fluid checks, filters, DOT inspections, and basic adjustments are your first line of defense. These services are relatively affordable compared to major repairs, yet they have the biggest impact on long-term reliability. Skipping preventive maintenance often leads to higher fleet maintenance expenses down the road, especially when small issues turn into roadside breakdowns.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-cost-breakdown-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Wear-and-Tear Components",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-breakdown-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Brakes, tires, belts, hoses, and suspension parts wear out by design. These costs are predictable and should be budgeted annually. Proactive replacement keeps your truck safer and helps maintain fuel efficiency.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-cost-breakdown-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Major Repairs",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-breakdown-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Engine work, transmission issues, aftertreatment systems, and electrical diagnostics account for the most expensive portion of semi truck maintenance costs. These repairs often result from deferred service, improper parts, or inconsistent maintenance records.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/the-real-average-maintenance-cost-for-a-semi-truck/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State International technician performing a preventive inspection on a semi truck's front axle"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-costs-vary",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Maintenance Costs Vary So Much",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-costs-vary"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-costs-vary-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "No two trucks are maintained the same way. Several factors influence the true average maintenance cost for a semi truck.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "features-why-costs-vary-2",
                  "type": "list",
                  "props": {
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "columns": 4,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Mileage & Duty Cycle",
                        "desc": "Long-haul trucks accumulate wear faster than regional or vocational units."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Truck Age",
                        "desc": "Older trucks typically require more frequent repairs."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Driver Habits",
                        "desc": "Aggressive driving increases wear on brakes, tires, and driveline components."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Service Quality",
                        "desc": "Experienced technicians catch problems earlier."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-costs-vary-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "And parts selection: OEM and high-quality aftermarket parts last longer and perform better. The difference between a $15,000 year and a $30,000 year often comes down to service decisions, not luck.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventive-maintenance",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive Maintenance: The Most Effective Cost-Control Tool",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventive-maintenance"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-maintenance-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive maintenance isn't just good practice; it's the most reliable way to lower truck operating costs over time. Regular inspections help identify issues before they become expensive repairs, reduce downtime, and extend the life of major components.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-maintenance-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're looking to stay ahead of repairs, our parts department carries the components you need to keep your trucks running right.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-preventive-maintenance-3-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-preventive-maintenance-3",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 26,
                          "paddingRight": 28,
                          "paddingBottom": 26,
